 \paragraph{Memory without a generative write.} Fidelity Before Structure \cite{fidelity} finds that verbatim chunks beat extracted artifacts and pools both in one list, whereas \sys{} gives each store its own share of the budget (Table~\ref{tab:extend}). EdgeMem \cite{edgemem}, like True Memory, builds memory with no generative call through one pipeline for every store, and LazyMem \cite{lazymem} defers construction to query time with a trained 4B model. \sys{} also writes with no generative call, trains nothing and adds detection, reading the configuration from each store's bytes.
 
-\paragraph{Choosing the cut, resolving conflicts, assembling.} Mix-of-Granularity \cite{mog}, AutoRAG \cite{autorag}, HiChunk \cite{hichunk}, FluxMem \cite{fluxmem} and Adaptive Chunking \cite{adaptivechunk} search for each store's RAG recipe by running every candidate, by labelled answers or by a trained model. OP-RAG \cite{oprag}, SeCom \cite{secom} and MacRAG \cite{macrag} assemble by order or by parent over preset or model-cut units, and other 2026 work resolves conflicts once they are known \cite{supersede,statefuse,tepa,lattice,toki,memlace,memtxn}. \sys{} instead measures two byte statistics once per store and sets the unit, the parent and the order from them, including whether an order exists at all, and resolves conflicts as a read-time view (Appendix~\ref{app:slotsrc}).
